[s0l0!-header][h1]Declarations Using Structures[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

To [b]declare variables[/b] of a structure data type, you use the keyword [b]struct[/b] followed by the struct tag, and then the variable name. 
For example, the statements below declares a structure data type and then uses the [b]student [/b]struct to declare variables [b]s1 [/b]and [b]s2[/b]:[code format="c" codeId="1762"]struct student {
  int age;
  int grade;
  char name[40];
};

/* declare two variables */
[b]struct student s1;[/b]
[b]struct student s2; [/b][/code]
[note]A struct variable is stored in a contiguous block of memory. The [b]sizeof[/b] operator must be used to get the number of bytes needed for a struct, just as with the basic data types.[/note]

